--  An object that a server keeps on behalf of a bank's holder, which
--  the bank's destruction reclaims (ADR 0014, section 3; #448).  The
--  server registers the object with the bank (Bank.Add_Dependent), and
--  keeps this cap with it.  When the bank, or a bank above it, is
--  destroyed, the storage server raises the signal that the server gave
--  it, and the server asks Destroyed of the dependents it holds, and
--  removes the objects whose banks are gone.
--
--  Release ends the registration, when the server removes the object
--  for its own reasons, and after it has removed one whose bank was
--  destroyed.  Registrations aren't saved in a checkpoint: a server
--  adds its dependents again when it is restored.

interface Dependent : Resource is

   function Destroyed return Boolean;
   --  True once the bank that the object was registered with has been
   --  destroyed.

end Dependent;
